NAME
    osarch-update - select the current host OS/architecture command roots

SYNOPSIS
    osarch-update

DESCRIPTION
    osarch-update is the compatibility command for detected-host platform
    selection. It is equivalent to:
        osarch-set

    The command detects the normalized operating system and architecture through
    the m OS/architecture facility, ensures the corresponding sys, ext and ai
    platform-specific bin directories exist and updates:
        bin/sys-osarch
        bin/ext-osarch
        bin/ai-osarch

    Existing non-symlink objects at selector paths are not overwritten.

    Use osarch-set <osarch> when a specific supported normalized OS/architecture
    identity must be selected explicitly.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Platform directories and selectors were updated.
    Non-zero status indicates unsupported platform data or filesystem/update
        failure.
